    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p15_b5",
      "text": "Table 21 isolates the contribution of each component. Re-\nmoving uncertainty weighting while retaining the topology\nreward degrades win-rate and increases ECE. Removing\nthe topology reward while retaining uncertainty weighting\npreserves some stability benefits but yields smaller improve-\nments in faithfulness. Setting the shaped reward weight to\nzero reduces TUR-DPO to weighted DPO, which improves\ncalibration but produces weaker structural gains. Replacing\nthe topology score with graph size confirms that perfor-\nmance is not explained by a trivial length prior. A listwise\nextension using four candidates per prompt yields an addi-\ntional, modest improvement.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.13,
        328.49,
        291.1,
        470.03
