      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p15_b24",
      "text": "We analyze sensitivity to the temperature parameter \u03b2, re-\nward mixing coefficient \u03b3, uncertainty penalty \u03bb, and the\nweight-mapping parameter \u03c4w. Figure 5 shows that perfor-\nmance is robust over broad parameter ranges. Increasing \u03b2\nsharpens the policy and can reduce win-rate if set too high.\nModerate values of \u03b3 provide the best trade-off between\nfaithfulness and diversity. Larger values of \u03bb down-weight\nuncertain pairs more aggressively and improve calibration\nup to a point, after which learning slows. The EMA refer-\nence decay parameter \u03c1 controls training stability; values\nbetween 0.99 and 0.997 perform well.\n",
      "bbox": [
